RF.put("questb:b69",{"8629":{"id":8629,"t":"Avenger's Legguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nSkin of the Great Sandworm Ouro\n2 Idol of Strife Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nAvenger's Legguards\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"Yes... the worm's skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we've destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Class Paladin Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8629\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Avenger's Legguards this quest\nBring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8709":{"id":8709,"t":"Dagger of Veiled Shadows","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Spiked Hilt, 2 Vermillion Idols, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Spiked Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Vermillion Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nDagger of Veiled Shadows\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8789":{"id":8789,"t":"Imperial Qiraji Armaments","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arygos in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj will create Elementium Infused Armaments for you should you bring him Imperial Qiraji Armaments and 3 Elementium Ore.\nImperial Qiraji Armaments\n3 Elementium Ore Blackwing Technician 7.7 % in Blackwing Lair","desc":"We have not sat idly by for a millennium, ‹name›.\nWe have watched these beasts feast on their own when they have exhausted their utility. We have listened as they have plotted and schemed to destroy our world. And we have learned of their own internal treachery.\nWeaknesses exist and we know how to use those weaknesses to our advantage.\nFind and bring me their ceremonial armaments: Combined with the element created from the volatility of their own God, they will become a force of reckoning.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlessed Qiraji War Axe Blessed Qiraji Musket Blessed Qiraji Pugio Blessed Qiraji Bulwark\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Seek out what I requested. You will become greater than the sum of your parts, champion.","done":"Infused with Elementium, these weapons will cut through the Qiraji and their God with incredible ease.\nUn'Goro Crater Open the zone on the world map Start Arygos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Arygos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8789","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8549":{"id":8549,"t":"The Horde Needs Peacebloom!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 54.","obj":"Bring 20 Peacebloom to Herbalist Proudfeather at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Peacebloom Peacebloom , Peacebloom , Rejold Barleybrew 50 % , Takar the Seer 40 % and 4 more","desc":"It is said that every generation must face a defining trial. I fear the Ahn'Qiraj War will be the crucible in which our mettle is tested. So we prepare, and in so doing find what we are made of.\nI have volunteered to help the Horde by gathering as much peacebloom as possible, so that it can be made into potions for the war. I hope that you are here to lend me your aid. If so, then I need you to bring back to me a good quantity of the herb. Will you assist me, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Go now, ‹class›. Seek out ‹name›.","done":"This was no easy task, yet you have excelled. But do not be too quick to think you have impressed me, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":33.1,"y":70.4,"n":"Herbalist Proudfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"1029":{"id":1029,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":28,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\nProvided: Dartol's Rod of Transformation","desc":"I suggest you find Raene and let her know the rod is finished. I'm sure she'll know what your next course should be.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"You've recreated the rod Teronis had set out to find? That's wonderful to hear.\nTeronis would be proud to see his quest is continuing even after his tragic passing.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":53.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Shael'dryn","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3509":{"id":3509,"t":"The Name of the Beast","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lord Arkkoroc in Azshara. Begin your search at the waters edge to find the Temple of Arkkoran.","desc":"There is only one way to harm the demon lord and his minions. A weapon of power must be forged bearing his true name.\nWhen such a weapon is forged, the demon and all under his command are vulnerable.\nA lesser deity resides in Azshara: Lord Arkkoroc. You must seek him out but be warned, his minions will stop at nothing to destroy you if you are discovered.\nUndoubtedly, you will have to pay a price for such information.","rew":"Experience: 6,200","done":"A demon lord?\n<Lord Arkkoroc laughs.>\nPerhaps the one can assist you with this information; but first, you must assist the one.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":77.1,"y":42.8,"n":"Lord Arkkoroc","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"8869":{"id":8869,"t":"Sweet Serenity","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme and kill the Crimson Hammersmith. Recover the Crimson Hammersmith's Apron and return to Lilith.\nCrimson Hammersmith's Apron Crimson Hammersmith","desc":"Within the confines of the Scarlet Bastion lies sweet Serenity. The Crimson Hammersmith guards the recipe with his life. Defeat him and bring me his apron. For that, I shall train you to become a hammersmith.\nUnderstand this: Once you have chosen the path of the hammersmith, the paths of the swordsmith and axesmith will no longer be available.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Enchanted Battlehammer\nExperience: 8,300\nLevel 60 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Profession Blacksmithing 0 Shareable Yes Quest ID 8869","cats":["blacksmithing"]},"96629":{"id":96629,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.6,"y":52.4,"n":"Gremlock Pilsnor","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94229":{"id":94229,"t":"Craftsmans writ ornate spyglass","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Ornate Spyglass\nOrnate Spyglass","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Ornate Spyglass, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","back":"Whoa! I almost didn't see you there. I might have seen you coming sooner if a damned engineer would at last deliver my order.","done":"Oh. Oh! You're the engineer? I suppose at the very least you are the delivery boy in any case.\nPlease hand over the spyglass. I have little time and many things to inspect.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":30.6,"y":60.9,"n":"Alan Sneeks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94309":{"id":94309,"t":"Craftsmans writ star belt","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Star Belt\nStar Belt","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Star Belt, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Star Belt Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94309","cats":["crafting"]},"949":{"id":949,"t":"The Twilight Camp","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a clue in the Twilight's Hammer camp at the Master's Glaive.","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer's purpose at the Master's Glaive is not known. But it must be dark.\nSearch through their camp at the Glaive... Search for some thing that may teach us their intentions.\nFor we must learn their intentions before a plan is made.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"This book is hand printed in an ancient language, and illustrated by a master artist.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.5,"y":86.1,"n":"Twilight Tome","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"8949":{"id":8949,"t":"Falrin's Vendetta","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 25 Ogre Warbeads from Ogres inside Dire Maul or Blackrock Spire and return to Falrin Treeshaper inside the Athenaeum in Dire Maul.\n25 Ogre Warbeads Gordok Bushwacker 40 % , Gordok Reaver 40 % , Gordok Warlock 40 % , Gordok Captain 40 % and 4 more","desc":"Yes, it is true that I am familiar with this enchantment you require, ‹class›. Yet I'm not one to give out favors freely, even if you were sent here by an old friend.\nI hold nothing but hatred and contempt for our brutish ogre neighbors. And not only them, I hate the followers of Omokk just as much as I hate those that follow King Gordok.\nI want you to kill them. Kill lots of them! Bring me the beads they carry around their neck as proof of your work. Do this and we shall talk about your request.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBeads of Ogre Might Beads of Ogre Mojo\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you performed the favor I asked of you, ‹name›?","done":"Hmmm... strangely enough I don't feel any better about my brother's death at the hands of those brutes.\nWell, you held your end of the bargain. Let's see what I can do for you.\nAlterac Mountains Silverpine Forest\nAlterac Mountains Open the zone on the world map Start Falrin Treeshaper End Falrin Treeshaper Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 8949\nThe chain\n44 quests at level 60, 90,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] One quest for each class\nDruid , Druid , Hunter , Mage , Paladin , Priest , Rogue , Warlock , Warrior , Hunter , Mage , Priest , Rogue , Shaman , Warlock , Warrior\nDeliana Dun Morogh\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] In Search of Anthion\nUse the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.\nDeliana Dun Morogh\n6,600 XP\n[ 60 ] In Search of Anthion\nUse the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.\nMokvar Orgrimmar\n6,600 XP\n3 [ 60 ] Dead Man's Plea\nGo into Stratholme and rescue Ysida Harmon from Baron Rivendare.\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n8,300 XP\n4 [ 60 ] Proof of Life\nBring Ysida's Locket to Anthion Harmon in Eastern Plaguelands.\nYsida Harmon\n6,600 XP\n5 [ 60 ] Anthion's Strange Request\nBring 3 Dark Iron Bars, 20 Enchanted Leather, 3 Mooncloth and 4 Cured Rugged Hides to Anthion Harmon in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n6,600 XP\n6 [ 60 ] Anthion's Old Friend\nTake the incomplete Banner of Provocation to Falrin Treeshaper at the library in Dire Maul.\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n6,600 XP\n7 [ 60 ] Falrin's Vendetta this quest\nCollect 25 Ogre Warbeads from Ogres inside Dire Maul or Blackrock Spire and return to Falrin Treeshaper inside the Athenaeum in Dire Maul.\nFalrin Treeshaper\n6,600 XP\n8 [ 60 ] The Instigator's Enchantment\nBring the following to Falrin Treeshaper inside Dire Maul: 1 Jeering Spectre's Essence, 4 Dark Runes and 8 Large Brilliant Shards.\nFalrin Treeshaper\n6,600 XP\n9 [ 60 ] The Challenge\nTravel to the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths and place the Banner of Provocation in its center as you are","cats":["dire-maul"]},"7429":{"id":7429,"t":"Free Knot!","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 56 instead of 57.","obj":"Gordok Shackle Key Gordok Bushwacker 24.5 % , Guard Fengus 13 % , Guard Slip'kik 13 % , Captain Kromcrush 13 % and 4 more","back":"It's called the Gordok Shackle Key - well, that's what these \"tons o' fun\" keep calling it. I think any of the ogres might have it, but I'm not sure if any specific ones do. Maybe the guards have a better chance of having one...\nWhat am I talking about - you have it already, don't you?! Is that it there??!","done":"Oh, thank you for freeing me! You - ranked number one. Everyone else - ranked number two or lower.\nI knew my life was destined for more than just being an appetizer to some ogre!\nAlterac Mountains Open the zone on the world map Start Knot Thimblejack End Knot Thimblejack Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7429\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 7,250 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Free Knot!\nKnot Thimblejack\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Free Knot! this quest\nKnot Thimblejack\n650 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"789":{"id":789,"t":"Sting of the Scorpid","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get 10 Scorpid Worker Tails for Gornek in the Den.\n10 Scorpid Worker Tail Sarkoth 80 % , Scorpid Worker 80 %","desc":"Powerful warrior and awkward novice alike have fallen to the venomous sting of the scorpid. You will find large numbers of scorpids northwest of here. Bring me ten of their tails as proof of your prowess in battle.\nThe antidote for their sting is actually made from venom extracted from their stingers. We keep large quantities of antidote for scorpid venom on hand to heal young bloods just like you...\nBut I'm sure you won't be needing any of that, will you?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSoft Wool Belt Battleworn Cape\nExperience: 250\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The carapace of a scorpid isn't so thick that the strength of a determined ‹class› will be deterred. Strike strongly and without doubt, and the scorpids should prove easy prey.","done":"There is an important lesson that you must take away from fighting scorpids. The smallest or largest of opponents can still send you to your doom. In fierce combat, any number of things can prove your downfall.\nI have no more to teach you, ‹name›. You have done well, and I will watch your progress with interest.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"149":{"id":149,"t":"Ghost Hair Thread","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Spectral Comb to Blind Mary.\nSpectral Comb\nProvided: Spectral Comb","desc":"There is a poor, sad spirit, Blind Mary, who haunts an old farm house in the hills south of Darkshire.\nHere, take this Spectral Comb and ask Blind Mary to comb her hair. Then bring back the comb and I will glean from it the Ghost Hair I'll need for the thread.\nAnd take care, for dark things now lurk near that house...","rew":"Experience: 490","back":"Oh please, don't look at me! I tore out these eyes with my own hands, but I can still feel your gaze!\nI'm hideous! Hideous! Please, look away!!","done":"What is this? A comb? It's lovely! And it glides through my hair as if it weren't the stiff, stringy horror that it is.\nOh, if only I had a mirror...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":82,"y":59.1,"n":"Blind Mary","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"69":{"id":69,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to The Lion's Pride Inn to see if anyone there has heard of the name Stalvan.","desc":"Oh my! Must have missed this the first time. In the registry, right beneath the first address for Stalvan there's another one listed, only partially scratched out. Looks like he was headed to The Lion's Pride Inn over in Goldshire. Might want to check there, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Stalvan? Sure sounds familiar.\nDuskwood Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.8,"y":65.8,"n":"Innkeeper Farley","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"229":{"id":229,"t":"The Daughter Who Lived","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Watcher Sarah Ladimore in Darkshire.","desc":"I should have told you this earlier...\nHow do I put this...\nMorgan may have believed that his family was all dead, but, in fact, his daughter Sarah Ladimore is now a Watcher. She's always been troubled by the... circumstances... surrounding her father's death. Perhaps you could go to bring the news to her.","rew":"Experience: 280\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Yes? My father...\n<Her eyes become downcast.>\nI wish... there was something I could have done for him... If only I had talked to him before he...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":74,"y":47.8,"n":"Watcher Ladimore","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1269":{"id":1269,"t":"Lieutenant Paval Reethe","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Reethe's Badge to Krog in Brackenwall Village.\nReethe's Badge\nProvided: Reethe's Badge","desc":"A glint of light on the ground catches your eye from underneath the rubble. Brushing debris and ash caked onto the object reveals the insignia of a gold anchor on white, enameled on the surface: the sign of Theramore.\nUnderneath the anchor is embossed the name \"Lieutenant Paval Reethe\".","rew":"Experience: 700","back":"Have you found any leads on what happened at the Shady Rest Inn?","done":"I know this human, Paval Reethe. Pathetic, even for his kind. He deserted his fellow soldiers and is now hiding out in the woods.\nI sent Ogron out to track him down. Some of the others suspect he's been stealing from our supplies. I think I saw Ogron heading off to the southeast.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":29.8,"y":48.2,"n":"Theramore Guard Badge","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5509":{"id":5509,"t":"Invader's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Invader's Scourgestone Lorekeeper Polkelt in Scholomance , Rattlegore in Scholomance , Blood Steward of Kirtonos in Scholomance , Terrordale Spirit 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops. These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands. Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil.\nThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia. Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nEach valor token handed out to worthy recipients is a sign of the tide turning against the Scourge. With more and more heroes fighting the Scourge in their own lands, the Argent Dawn will assuredly be at the forefront when the time comes to wage war on the ultimate evil of the Scourge. I hope that the valor you've shown what it took to acquiring your token will carry the day then as well!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"8469":{"id":8469,"t":"Beads for Salfa","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 575 experience instead of 550, 1.05 times as much.","obj":"The Winterfall are known to carry spirit beads to ward against foul spirits. These beads have clearly failed in their purpose, as the Winterfall themselves are the agents of corruption. Bring to me these spirit beads from fallen Winterfall furbolgs; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.\n5 Winterfall Spirit Beads Winterfall Runner 30 % , High Chief Winterfall 30 % , Winterfall Shaman 30 % , Winterfall Ursa 30 % and 3 more","rew":"Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"You've certainly earned my trust, ‹name›, but you may need to continue to earn the trust of my untrusting tribe. There is something you can do to earn that trust.\nThe Winterfall are known to carry spirit beads to ward against foul spirits. These beads have clearly failed in their purpose, as the Winterfall themselves are the agents of corruption. Bring to me these spirit beads from fallen Winterfall furbolgs; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.","done":"Once again, you prove your honor to us! I will make sure that your deeds are known amongst my kind.\nRemember to bring any of the Winterfall's beads you find to me. For each set you continue to bring to me, I will speak on your behalf to the tribe.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":27.7,"y":34.5,"n":"Salfa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2869":{"id":2869,"t":"Against the Hatecrest","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Hatecrest Naga Scales to Latronicus Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n10 Hatecrest Naga Scale Hatecrest Screamer 55 % , Hatecrest Warrior 55 % , Lady Szallah 40 % , Lord Shalzaru 40 % and 4 more","desc":"The best course of action at this point is to assume that, regardless of what the naga are up to, they will eventually move to secure the island for their own. We need to take aggressive steps to counter that threat before it is too late.\nBring me ten Hatecrest Scales that are in good condition; it should be obvious to you how to acquire them. You'll cut your teeth on the naga for the first time, and we'll have a weakened naga presence on Sardor Isle - both are prospects that play to our advantage.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, if you're here to verify the task given to you, then excellent - it is ten Hatecrest scales I seek. If you are here for chit-chat, then I am currently unavailable for such trivialities.\nKnow this - we night elves are not warmongers. Our race is dedicated to the preservation of peace and harmony. This does not mean, however, that we will not proactively protect our own interests. This is my duty to General Feathermoon, and to the stronghold.","done":"Yes, yes, these scales are more than satisfactory. Actually, I think I will send these down to Pratt for him to take a look at. Maybe he can craft something useful out of them.\nAs for you, I have another mission I want to send you on. But first, here is your bounty for the scales. Your continued service to the General and Feathermoon Stronghold at large is a blessing in the face of adversity.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"8229":{"id":8229,"t":"Could I get a Fishing Flier?","lv":60,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 55.","rew":"You will receive:\nFishing Tournament!","done":"There is a Fishing Contest in Booty Bay this Sunday! Here are the rules for you!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.5,"y":72.8,"n":"Grinkle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"2949":{"id":2949,"t":"Return of the Ring","lv":34,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You may either keep the ring, or you may find the person responsible for the imprint and engravings on the inside of the band.\nBrilliant Gold Ring\nProvided: Brilliant Gold Ring","desc":"Opening the box produced by the Sparklematic 5200 reveals a shiny ring! Donning the ring, you feel magic power surge through your body.\nInside the band is a small but nonetheless discernable imprint of the seal of Orgrimmar. Engraved letters are next to it, but only the first three stand out even after cleaning: \"NOG...\"\nThis may signify either the initials of the previous owner, or perhaps the initials of the ring's crafter. Keep the ring... or find \"NOG\" - decisions, decisions...","rew":"Experience: 2,700","back":"You'd think that we would find a way on our own to outdo those filthy little gnomes. I would even wager that they stole that rig from us to begin with! Bah, those greasy, grimy... erm, yes? You need something?","done":"A ring from Gnomeregan? Let's see... not mine, but interesting.\nThe Gnomeregan thing - couldn't have happened to a nicer bunch of numbskulls. For years they're a joke, and now almost overnight they're making better rigs than us?\nDark Iron dwarves had the ring? That's even more interesting! You know, maybe the gnomes stole their crazy golem plans and modified them. Those Dark Irons, they'd definitely want some major payback. It's certainly worth investigating.\nYou know, about that ring...","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":76,"y":25.4,"n":"Nogg","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"549":{"id":549,"t":"WANTED: Syndicate Personnel","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Criminal's Pauldrons. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Kill 10 Syndicate Rogues and 10 Syndicate Watchmen. Return to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill for your reward.\nSyndicate Rogue slain : 0/ 10\nSyndicate Watchman slain : 0/ 10","desc":"By the authority of Lady Sylvanas, all members of the organization known as the Syndicate are wanted dead. Those brought into custody or taken prisoner will be summarily executed. They are currently known to be amassing in the ruins of Durnholde Keep, to the southeast of Tarren Mill.\nA handsome reward is offered to all who bring proof of their deeds to High Executor Darthalia.","rew":"New in Forever: Criminal's Pauldrons.\nYou will receive:\nCriminal's Pauldrons\nMoney: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have nothing better to do than stand here before me, ‹class›? As High Executor, I have more pressing matters than to stare at your rotting visage.","done":"Excellent, ‹class›. At this rate, the Syndicate pest will be rid from the land in no time.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.8,"n":"WANTED","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6069":{"id":6069,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thotar at Razor Hill.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Thotar at Razor Hill. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time for you to begin your training.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":68,"y":17.8,"n":"Sian'dur","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9269":{"id":9269,"t":"Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,300, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris wants you to take Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian to Stratholme and use it on Consecrated Earth. Defeat the entity that is exorcised from the staff and return to him.\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nAtiesh Cleansed\nProvided: Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","desc":"This final task will be the most difficult of all, ‹name›. You have faced and defeated both an Old God and the Lich King's General, but now you must face the hand of Sargeras.\nTake the staff to Stratholme. It is there that you will find a piece of consecrated earth: ground where the greatest knights of Lordaeron were murdered. Place the befouled staff upon the holy ground and prepare for an entity of immense power to break from within... Defeat the demonic being that controls the staff and return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"309":{"id":309,"t":"Protecting the Shipment","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ensure Miran and the shipment arrive at the excavation site, then inform Prospector Ironband.","desc":"Ready to go, ‹name›?\nFirst, we need to get this powder to Ironband. It'll be a lot for me to carry, and these parts can get dangerous -- and who knows what else the Dark Irons might have in store for me.\nI'll feel a lot better with you coming along.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nForeman Belt Mud Stompers\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Where is my powder, ‹name›? My need grows more desperate every day.","done":"Oh, thank the Light the powder is here. But it is troubling news that you bring as well. To think that the Dark Irons have sympathizers able to procure this sort of material for their dastardly plans.\nThat's a matter for someone else to consider, some other time. I must put this powder to good use.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":52.2,"y":69.4,"n":"Miran","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.9,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"7029":{"id":7029,"t":"Vyletongue Corruption","lv":47,"min":41,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Coated Cerulean Vial at the orange crystal pool in Maraudon.\nUse the Filled Cerulean Vial on the Vylestem Vines to force the corrupted Noxxious Scion to emerge.\nHeal 8 plants by killing these Noxxious Scion, then return to Vark Battlescar in Shadowprey Village.\nFilled Cerulean Vial\nVylestem Vines healed : 0/ 8\nProvided: Coated Cerulean Vial","desc":"A satyr known as Vyletongue has corrupted the caverns of Maraudon, stunting the growth of many of the plants inside.\nTake this vial, ‹name›. Fill it at the orange crystal pool found inside the caverns; the coating inside the vial will counter the toxins, turning it into a healing agent.\nFind the Vylestem vines inside the orange caverns, and use the purified liquid on them. The corruption will be purged from the plant, but do know that Vyletongue will still control it. He may use it against you...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWoodseed Hoop Sagebrush Girdle Branchclaw Gauntlets\nExperience: 5,250","back":"If you are able to heal the plant, it will again begin to grow. We must do what we can, ‹name›...","done":"Thank you for returning this, ‹name›. With the remaining liquid you brought me, I can continue my studies.\nWhile there is still much to do, you have helped to heal some of the corruption that Vyletongue spread through Maraudon. Please take this with my gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":23.2,"y":70.3,"n":"Vark Battlescar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"9109":{"id":9109,"t":"Plagueheart Belt","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Plagueheart Belt if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Belt, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Arcane Crystals and 2 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Belt Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Belt\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Belt.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"7509":{"id":7509,"t":"The Forging of Quel'Serrar","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You must get Onyxia to breathe fire on the Unfired Ancient Blade. Once this is done, pick up the now Heated Ancient Blade. Be warned, a Heated Ancient Blade will not remain heated forever - time is of the essence.\nThe last step before returning to me is to slay the beast and drive the Heated Ancient Blade into her corpse.\nDo this and Quel'Serrar will be yours.\nTreated Ancient Blade\nProvided: Unfired Ancient Blade","desc":"Take the unfired ancient blade to the lair of Onyxia and engage her in battle.\nSome trickery must be utilized for the heating of the blade. While in combat, she will surely try to incinerate you with her fiery breath. You must plant the unfired ancient blade nearby and hope that the fiery breath heats the blade. If you live beyond this, pick up the now heated ancient blade and finish off the dragon.\nPlunge the heated ancient blade into her smoldering corpse to fashion the treated ancient blade.","rew":"You will receive:\nQuel'Serrar\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"Perhaps one day, another will wield the prismatic blade.","done":"<Lydros murmurs something unintelligible.>\nAs promised, ‹class›, the blade of Quel'Serrar.\nStart Lorekeeper Lydros End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7509\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 60, 26,950 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Foror's Compendium\nReturn Foror's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the Athenaeum.\nNostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Forging of Quel'Serrar\nGive the Dull and Flat Elven Blade to Lorekeeper Lydros.\nA Dull and Flat Elven Blade\n7,050 XP\n3 [ 60 ] The Forging of Quel'Serrar this quest\nYou must get Onyxia to breathe fire on the Unfired Ancient Blade.\nLorekeeper Lydros\n9,950 XP","cats":["onyxias-lair"]},"1109":{"id":1109,"t":"Going, Going, Guano!","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 pile of Kraul Guano to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.\nKraul Guano Greater Kraul Bat 80 % in Razorfen Kraul , Kraul Bat 80 % in Razorfen Kraul","desc":"As you can see, ‹name›, we're up to some very.... interesting experiments at the Royal Apothecary Society.\nAs the Master here, it is my job to oversee the most ambitious of our alchemical attempts. So much work and so little time!\nYou look well traveled for a ‹class›. Perhaps you can aid me.\nI'm in need of a rare substance. It's foul material; it comes from a rare species of bats only found in the muck-hole known as Razorfen Kraul. Bring to me the guano from the Kraul Bats so we can begin our work...","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Ah, I see you have returned. Were you able to procure any Kraul Guano?","done":"Splendid! This is just the start we needed, ‹name›.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-kraul"]},"3109":{"id":3109,"t":"Encrypted Rune","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Rune and speak to Solm Hargrin in Coldridge Valley.\nEncrypted Rune\nProvided: Encrypted Rune","desc":"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the rogue trainer Solm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You made it! Great!\nWe've got an influx of activity lately, so I'm glad to count another of the Ironforge clan among our numbers. Too many of us are lookin' to the arcane, and divine for my own tastes. Nothin' against them and their beliefs, but there's nothing like a cold blade in your hand and a shadow to keep you from the light, know what I mean?","done":"Anyway, as you start peekin' around Coldridge you'll probably have need of training at some point. You just come back to me whenever you feel you need it and I'll teach you what I know--a trick here, a maneuver there. You know, the stuff that keeps you alive and makin' a little extra coin.\nKeep an eye out on our gnomish friends too... they kinda got the short end of the stick what with Gnomeregan being... destroyed. They'll need our help to feel welcome.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.4,"y":67.5,"n":"Solm Hargrin","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"95189":{"id":95189,"t":"Crest of lordaeron","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Return the Crest of Lordaeron to Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City.\nProvided: Crest of Lordaeron","desc":"<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in Stormwind would be very keen to get their hands on this.>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSmall Sack of Gems\nExperience: 6,200","back":"Welcome to the gallery. Feel free to browse.","done":"How in the world did you find this? It's in such remarkable condition... all things considered.\nThank you for restoring this piece of Alliance history, ‹class›. I'll have my best people get to work restoring this immediately.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.8,"y":28.6,"n":"Lady Dena Kennedy","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"9029":{"id":9029,"t":"A Bubbling Cauldron","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlue Dinner Suit Purple Dinner Suit Red Dinner Suit Lovely Blue Dress Lovely Purple Dress Lovely Red Dress","done":"A pleasant smell wafts up from the cauldron.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":89.6,"y":75.7,"n":"Fragrant Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8149":{"id":8149,"t":"Honoring a Hero","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Uther's Tomb in Western Plaguelands and use Uther's Tribute at his statue, and then return to Wagner Hammerstrike outside Ironforge before the Harvest Festival is over.\nProvided: Uther's Tribute","desc":"During the Harvest Festival of Azeroth, we give thanks to heroes for the sacrifices - in some cases ultimate sacrifices - they have given on our behalf. The Alliance acknowledges many heroes, but none weave a more tragic tale than that of Uther Lightbringer.\nHelp us honor Uther by taking this offering to his tomb in the Western Plaguelands. Place it at his statue, and then return to me. I'll only be here through the end of the festival, so waste no time in giving Uther his tribute.","rew":"You will receive:\nFor the Light!\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Alliance","back":"Have you made the journey to Uther's Tomb and placed the tribute there?\nIt can be a dangerous trip for less experienced adventurers; a safer way of traveling there, relatively speaking, may be to travel north from the river that runs through Hillsbrad into the Plaguelands. It flows from a lake that is adjacent to Sorrow Hill; travel west up through the hills, steering clear of the adjacent tomb... one that is infested with the Scourge.","done":"He was a hero among heroes, Uther was. I can't even begin to imagine the anguish of what he felt when Arthas - his greatest student and someone whom Uther loved like his own son - betrayed all of humanity. Still, he rose to try and stop Arthas, and for that he will be forever remembered as a true paladin. His fight was to the end, thinking only of those he might save.\nThank you, ‹name›. You've paid tribute to a great hero today, honoring his spirit and the spirit of the Harvest Festival.\nDun Morogh Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":52.6,"y":36,"n":"Wagner Hammerstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94789":{"id":94789,"t":"Call of air","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Veyric Thundervein in Arathi Highlands.","desc":"The winds o' Azeroth greet ye, and soon ye'll stand among some o' our mightiest kin. I'm proud to see how far ye've come--your future looks bright indeed.\nThe element o' air's a tricky one to master, but I've faith your skill will see ye through any challenge.\nMake your way north into Arathi Highlands. In its northern hills, you'll find Veyric Thundervein. He'll teach ye more.","rew":"You will receive:\nAir Totem\nExperience: 2,450\nIronforge Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":47.4,"y":13.6,"n":"Eldrun Stormbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":59.8,"y":27.6,"n":"Veyric Thunderhame","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"7669":{"id":7669,"t":"Again into the great ossuary","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nDivination Scryer","done":"Are you headed back into the Scholomance, ‹name›? You've already paid such a great price for the use of the Divination Scryer - perhaps you'd like to take another one with you. With it, you'd be able to face the perils of the Great Ossuary once more.\nBy all means, have it. You've certainly earned it.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.6,"y":36.2,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8309":{"id":8309,"t":"Glyph Chasing","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 2g 70s instead of 1g 80s. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,800, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Rutgar Glyphshaper at Bronzebeard's Encampment in Silithus wants you to venture to Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal and recover Glyphed Rubbings from the Glyphed Crystals of each hive.\nUse the Geologist's Transcription Kit to make a reasonable facsimile of the ancient glyphs. Return to Rutgar Glyphshaper when you complete this task.\nHive'Ashi Rubbing\nHive'Zora Rubbing\nHive'Regal Rubbing\nGeologist's Transcription Kit\nProvided: Geologist's Transcription Kit","desc":"After our initial foray into the hives and Mistress Mar'alith's subsequent madness the three hives have been spewing out bugs! The increased activity might be tied into the glyphs covering those strange crystals.\nWe must get a rubbing from crystals in all three hives. If we can get those rubbings, we might be able to make sense of this madness.\nTake this transcription set and hit those hives, ‹name›. Don't come back until you've gotten copies from each hive.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"If you find some crazy night elf lass in one of the hives, be sure to give her a kick in the duff for us.","done":"I can't make heads or tails of these glyphs. I've never seen anything like it! I hope Frankal's research can shed some light on this mess.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":41.3,"y":88.5,"n":"Rutgar Glyphshaper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78149":{"id":78149,"t":"Fury of the land","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Fury of the Land","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nFury of the Land (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"6629":{"id":6629,"t":"Kill Grundig Darkcloud","lv":18,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Grundig Darkcloud and 6 Grimtotem Brutes, and return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.\nGrundig Darkcloud slain\nGrimtotem Brute slain : 0/ 6","desc":"‹name›, you've done a fine job killing Grimtotem. If you dare, Grundig Darkcloud and his personal band of brutes is by far the worst of the lot. He was the one who led the brutal attack on my village.\nYou will find him in Grimtotem Post a bit further up the path to the west. Kill him, and I will be forever grateful.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350","back":"Have you killed Grundig Darkcloud and his personal band of Brutes?","done":"Grundig Darkcloud is dead! ‹name›, I will always be grateful for what you've done here today.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.2,"y":27.8,"n":"Makaba Flathoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"389":{"id":389,"t":"Bazil Thredd","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Warden Thelwater in the Stockade.","desc":"VanCleef and I were members of the Stonemasons Guild. Our main project was to rebuild Stormwind after the War.\nWhen we had finished our duties, we were cheated. The nobles refused to pay us for our work. Some of the more senior of the Stonemasons were offered governmental jobs, but VanCleef refused it out of loyalty to all the Stonemasons. He led a riot and left the city, swearing revenge.\nHis lieutenant, Bazil Thredd, might know more about VanCleef's plans. He's being held prisoner in the Stockade.","rew":"Experience: 440","done":"What in the Light do you want? Can't you see we have a crisis here?\nBazil Thredd?! Why would you want to speak with that bastard? How am I supposed to know you're not one of his cronies, come down to help with his bloody riot? If all the blasted cells weren't open, I might throw you in one for a while!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.5,"y":69.4,"n":"Warden Thelwater","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"629":{"id":629,"t":"The Vile Reef","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Tablet Shard to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\nTablet Shard Gri'lek the Wanderer , Gri'lek the Wanderer","desc":"Long ago, a great shudder of the earth sunk an old troll city beneath the waters of the Savage Coast to the northwest. We call that place the Vile Reef, for murlocs now reside in the ruins of the city, attacking any who draw close.\nThere is an old tablet among those ruins that tells the ancient tale of Gri'lek, a hero of troll legends. The tale is sacred to the Darkspear tribe, and although the tablet is too large to move, I want a shard of it to enshrine in our new home in Orgrimmar.","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I await the Tablet Shard, ‹name›.","done":"This is good. When I return to Orgrimmar I will place this shard in a sacred place. It will remind us of the might and honor of Gri'lek.\nThank you, ‹name›. Your deeds mark a growing friendship with the Darkspear tribe.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8069":{"id":8069,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Illusionist's Robes","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Kossack. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Kossack\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The tribe acknowledges station and power through what we wear. Our vestments are made from the finest of materials, and interwoven with the mojo we use to make us powerful. Illusionists are no exception; their robes are said to embody the essence of illusion in their look. Legend states that their ancient robes never looked the same twice.\nI will give you an illusionist's robe, ‹name›... but earn your place of reverence among the tribe first! Bring me the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Illusionist's Robe\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have you returned with the Paragons of Power we need? I know it will not be easy... but I have long predicted an outsider would come to aid us in our fight against Hakkar. Let it be you, I say!","done":"At last, someone worthy to wear the illusionist's robe! Your success in Zul'Gurub has assured your reverences amongst the tribe for ages to come. Wear it with pride, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"93429":{"id":93429,"t":"Blood of my blood","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 10 Lost Ones in the Fallow Sanctuary.\nLost One slain (10) Lost One Hunter Lost One Seer Lost One Lost One Muckdweller Lost One Riftseeker\nLost One Hunter\nLost One Seer\nLost One\nLost One Muckdweller\nLost One Riftseeker","desc":"Although they are our kin, the Lost Ones of Fallow Sanctuary have become beings of pure violence and hatred.\nThere can be no redemption or salvation for them. They are doomed to wander this swamp as mindless, hateful creatures for all their lives.\nTheir suffering must end. Someone must put them out of their misery. A grisly task, I know, but would you do it to protect those of us who remain?","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nSwamp of Sorrows Open the zone on the world map Level 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93429","cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"1429":{"id":1429,"t":"The Atal'ai Exile","lv":44,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Bundle of Atal'ai Artifacts to the Atal'ai Exile in the Hinterlands.\nBundle of Atal'ai Artifacts\nProvided: Bundle of Atal'ai Artifacts","desc":"While you were braving the dangers of the Pool of Tears, one of my scouts returned with a scroll written in blood on dried flesh. It seems to be a judicial sentence against a priest of the Atal'ai tribe.\nThis priest was sentenced to a fate worse than death amongst the Atal'ai.\nHe was exiled to live far north in the Hinterlands, with the Witherbark trolls.\nI will bundle these artifacts. You are to seek out the exile and discover their true use. Return to me once your journey is complete.","rew":"Experience: 3,750","back":"You are brave to come here. Brave or foolish...","done":"You bring me the summoning artifacts of the Atail'ai?\nI see Jammal'an the Prophet is leading the disciples of the Chamber of Blood towards their chosen fate. Has Hakkar returned to the Temple I wonder? Has their fate been met?\nSwamp of Sorrows The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.9,"y":54.8,"n":"Fel'zerul","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":33.8,"y":75.2,"n":"Atal'ai Exile","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"869":{"id":869,"t":"Raptor Thieves","lv":13,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Raptor Heads to Gazrog at the Crossroads.\n12 Raptor Head Ishamuhale , Sunscale Lashtail 80 % , Sunscale Screecher 80 % , Sunscale Scytheclaw 80 % and 1 more","desc":"Not long ago, a shipment of silver was stolen from our guard tower. It was meant as payroll to the Crossroads' guards, and we want that silver back.\nThe strange thing is... we caught one of the thieves on the night of the theft. And... it was a raptor! Unbelievable!\nI don't know what raptors would want with silver. But I don't care -- I want the raptors dead so they won't steal from us again!\nHunt raptors in the Barrens. Collect for me their heads!","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have those heads, ‹name›?","done":"You got rid of the raptors!\nThank you, ‹name›. You are a ‹class› of worth.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.9,"y":30.3,"n":"Gazrog","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7829":{"id":7829,"t":"Hunt the Savages","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Markhor at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill 20 Savage Owlbeasts. Return to him once the task is complete.\nMarkhor mentioned that the Savage Owlbeasts occupy the wilds of the Hinterlands.\nSavage Owlbeast slain : 0/ 20","desc":"Among the more ornery of the wildlife of the Hinterlands are the savage owlbeasts. Many a good Revantusk warrior has been lost to the ferocious claws and beak of the beasts.\nKill every savage owlbeast you see, ‹race›. Return to me when you can stand no more bloodshed. Your contribution will then be weighed, measured, and judged.","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Clear your head of impure thoughts, ‹race›. Become one with the wilds!","done":"You have proven a worthy ally to the Revantusk, ‹name›. Well done.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.2,"y":79.5,"n":"Huntsman Markhor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"98069":{"id":98069,"t":"Stolen freewind supplies","lv":31,"min":27,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 8 Stolen Freewind Supplies to Jandia in Freewind Post.\n8 Stolen Freewind Supplies","desc":"Those wretched harpies! They attacked the last caravan I had scheduled to deliver supplies to Freewind Post. We have enough supplies for the moment, but without more supplies, we'll run short soon.\nI'm not sure what the harpies plan to do with the extra supplies, but I would be grateful if you would recover them for me. They make their lair west of here. They can be found both at the base of the cliffside and inside a cave at the top.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":46,"y":51.4,"n":"Jandia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1189":{"id":1189,"t":"Safety First","lv":41,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Modified Seaforium Booster to Razzeric on the Shimmering Flats.\nModified Seaforium Booster\nProvided: Modified Seaforium Booster","desc":"There, I did what Razzeric wanted. Just tell him to be careful when he sets this off. If he makes the slightest mistake, he won't be moving forward, he'll just be a burnt spot on the track.\nWould be a shame, too, if that happened. Who knows if our nineteenth driver would be any good?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRazzeric's Customized Seatbelt Razzeric's Racing Grips\nExperience: 825\n+25 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Can you believe Pozzik put a bucket of sand on the racer? How am I supposed to hit my maximum speed with a bucket of sand under the seat?","done":"Now that's more like it! I wish I could see the look on the gnomes' eyes when they see me set this baby off.\nToo bad I'll be too busy pulling off a new course record!\nTanaris Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51,"y":27.2,"n":"Shreev","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.3,"y":76.1,"n":"Razzeric","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"98389":{"id":98389,"t":"A light in the darkness","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Free 6 Webbed Victims in Night's Web Hollow for Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell.\nWebbed Forsaken freed : 0/ 6","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. Yes, I am a paladin. Not even death can stop the Light.\nThis is something my kind have in common with all Forsaken--we have overcome what the living view as their end. However, some even among our own fear us; they suspect we will smite them as some monstrosity.\nIn truth, our relationship with undeath is complex, but I am not here to hurt our own. Help me show the others this. Venture to Night's Web Hollow to the northwest and free the freshly raised fools trapped by the spiders there.","done":"May this help Executor Arren and so many others see our true nature. Much like in our past lives, we live to serve our people--to protect them with the gifts the Light provides us.\nThey will see in time that we are just as valuable to the Dark Lady's plans as any other.\nLight be with you.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31.1,"y":66.3,"n":"Aramis Hammerhand","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31,"y":66.2,"n":"Aramis Hammerhand","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"709":{"id":709,"t":"Solution to Doom","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Doomcaller's Pants, Fists of Impending Doom.","obj":"Bring the Tablet of Ryun'eh to Theldurin the Lost.\nTablet of Ryun'eh Ancient Chest","desc":"Oh my! Oh my! There is a doom approaching. Mark me! A doom!\nNo, I cannot speak of it...cannot utter their names or they may hear me! But if we learn, yes, if we learn more of them...then maybe we can learn how to foil them!\nMaybe.\nGo into Uldaman. No! I said it! You must find...find the tablet of...Ryun'eh. Yes, find it! And don't make me speak that name again!\nIt is deep in that place, in an ancient chest. That's where it hides...in a chest crafted before the works of any dwarf.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDoomsayer's Robe Doomcaller's Pants Fists of Impending Doom\nNew in Forever: Doomcaller's Pants, Fists of Impending Doom.\nExperience: 3,150","back":"Did you find the tablet? It must hold secrets! Secrets to save us!","done":"Oh, fortune is with us! Thank you! We may yet be saved!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3909":{"id":3909,"t":"The Videre Elixir","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Gregan Brewspewer in northern Feralas. From him, learn how you may acquire the Videre Elixir, then return to Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\nVidere Elixir","desc":"Now, what's this? Linken... FORGOT?\nOh, I see... Lost his memory...\nWell, here is his sword. It's not complete, though. I know of the one that can finish it, but... speaking with him may prove difficult.\nListen, I know of someone that will be able to help you. It's too much to explain right now, but you must somehow acquire a Videre Elixir. The only one I know that can help you with that is Gregan Brewspewer. He's hard to track down, but last I knew he was camping in the wilds of Feralas.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Back already?","done":"I'll need one vial to make sure that this is truly the elixir... Yes... This is the stuff.\nWinterspring Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1509":{"id":1509,"t":"News of Dogran","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Gazrog at the Crossroads.","desc":"My mate, Dogran, was recently sent to the Crossroads for duty. It was a promotion, and he was very proud.\nI was sad, of course, but I didn't let him know that. And worried, too. The Barrens is a more dangerous place than Orgrimmar, and I feared the worst.\nNow it's been a week after he should have returned, and I have received no word from him...\nPerhaps you could go to the Crossroads and see if they have any news? He worked with Gazrog, who should still be stationed there.","rew":"Experience: 390","done":"Zankaja? That's Dogran's mate, right?\nYeah, I've heard from him, but it's not the sort of news we should let get back to her...\nNo, he's not dead. But he is injured and a prisoner of the quilboar.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37,"y":59.4,"n":"Zankaja","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.9,"y":30.3,"n":"Gazrog","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8389":{"id":8389,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Experience: 725\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"6389":{"id":6389,"t":"A Plague Upon Thee","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Release the Plagueland Termites in the Northridge Lumber Mill, then return with the Barrel of Plagueland Termites to Nathaniel Dumah at Chillwind Camp in Western Plaguelands.\nBarrel of Plagueland Termites\nProvided: Barrel of Plagueland Termites","desc":"You look around the lumber mill for something suitable to open the barrel with. You find a crowbar that looks like it will do the trick.\nYou set your feet and pray that you'll be able to get out of the mill before the termites get to you.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Have you done it, ‹name›? Have you released the termites? The Light help us if the Scarlet Crusade were able to hold onto both the mill and Hearthglen. They should have neither. They're just capitalizing on the victims of the last war and should be put down like rabid animals!","done":"Haha! Thank you, ‹name›! You've done it! My father's spirit can now rest and I can live in peace.\nThank you again. If there is anything I can do for you, please, just ask.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":48.3,"y":32,"n":"Termite Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.4,"y":84.8,"n":"Nathaniel Dumah","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"469":{"id":469,"t":"Daily Delivery","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Bundle of Crocolisk Skins to James Halloran, the tanner, in Menethil Harbor.\nBundle of Crocolisk Skins\nProvided: Bundle of Crocolisk Skins","desc":"Greetings, traveler!\nDon't suppose you might be heading in the direction of Menethil, would you? If you're not, I'd suggest you stop there, it's a good place to purchase goods and even have a pint and relax.\nNow, if it just so happens that you're heading in that direction, I don't suppose you'd mind taking this bundle of crocolisk skins to James Halloran, the tanner?\nI'd do it myself, but my wife's been in quite a mood lately, and I'd like to put off facing her as long as possible.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello there, ‹class›. Could I interest you in a pair of boots? Perhaps some newly cured skins?","done":"Hmm, this is from Einar, right? Hasn't delivered his skins to me in person for almost a week now. No doubt it's some differences with the wife!\nMaybe I'll have my wife go speak with Sida sometime...","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.9,"y":39.4,"n":"Einar Stonegrip","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.5,"y":55.7,"n":"James Halloran","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92469":{"id":92469,"t":"Return to rorian","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring word of the Al'Aketh to Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.","desc":"You've done enough here, ‹class›. I'll stay and clean up any stragglers down there.\nHead back to the Village and tell Rorian about the cult's presence. He will not be pleased.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWindblown Short Cloak Skychain Belt\nExperience: 35","done":"This is most troubling, but unfortunately unsurprising. We've been aware of the cult's movements for some time, but we've been content to watch from afar. Their agitation of the wind spirits near the standing stones is a clear escalation on their part.\nYou've performed a difficult but necessary service for Thendal Grove, Ranir. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":47.2,"y":21.8,"n":"Yala Windwatcher","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92709":{"id":92709,"t":"A grand adventure","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Listen to what Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar has to say.\nListen to Elaadrin","desc":"Your highborne lineage shines as clearly in your eyes as the sky above. You are one of us, and its youth like yourself that will help us save our home. But first, let me tell you more of our mission and plans here on Zephras... and beyond.","done":"So do you now see? Rediscovering the ancient magic of our forebears is the key to unlocking the secrets of Zephras Isle and securing our future, but in order to save our home, we must rediscover what we've lost these past millennia.\nAzeroth is the key. The Kirin Tor will show us the way.\nWhile we make ready to leave, you should check in with the other members of the High Order here in Valanaar. Most of them have tasks that they could use help from one such as yourself to see completed.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"95349":{"id":95349,"t":"The earthen ring","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Mulgore and speak with Alana Stormwalker when you arrive.","desc":"The recent events with the cult have delayed my plans to travel to Azeroth and I must remain here in Valanaar for a time. You and a handful of other Windshapers will be our vanguard instead. Alaana Stormwalker will be waiting to receive you upon your arrival in Mulgore, and I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we finish our business here. We will join you soon.\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there. Banu-Alah, ‹name›.","done":"More adventurers from Zephras, I see. Wonderful. The winds surely favor us! It's going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore this new land.\nAzeroth is an exciting new world, but it's also a dangerous world. You'd do well to prepare yourself for this new adventure by familiarizing yourself with the lands nearby.\nZephras Isle Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Alaana Stormwalker","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});